    <string-array name="nutrition_tips">
        <item>Stay well hydrated. Water improves your performance and your recovery.</item>
        <item>Include a source of protein in every meal: it helps your muscles recover after training.</item>
        <item>Fill half your plate with vegetables: they provide fiber, vitamins and fullness.</item>
        <item>Legumes are cheap and complete: protein, fiber and slow-release carbs.</item>
        <item>A piece of fruit is an easy snack before training.</item>
        <item>Sleeping well is nutrition too: rest regulates appetite and recovery.</item>
        <item>Choose whole grains when you can: more fiber and steadier energy.</item>
        <item>Nuts are healthy; a handful a day is a good serving.</item>
        <item>Planning the week\'s meals avoids improvising with ultra-processed food.</item>
        <item>After training, combine protein and carbs to recover better.</item>
        <item>Varying the colors on your plate is an easy way to vary nutrients.</item>
        <item>Carry a water bottle with you: drinking becomes automatic.</item>
    </string-array>
